(5817427, 846048, 83313, '<td valign="top">This needs Godzilla rising up out of the ocean to make it complete. I have no idea whose entry this is. I seem to not be familiar with as many individual styles as I thought.</td>', 'This needs Godzilla rising up out of the ocean to make it complete. I have no idea whose entry this is. I seem to not be familiar with as many individual styles as I thought.', '2010-01-18 22:02:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5817436, 845220, 83313, '<td valign="top">This is obviously from someone who has never gotten one of my infamous JPEG comments before. So, here you go...<br/> <br/>There are a ton of compression artifacts showing around the edges of the tower. A 39k file size confirms excessive compression is what is killing the detail and clarity in this shot. Compression kills detail. Always use the least amount of compression you can get away with and still come in under the challenge limit.<br/> <br/>Other than that it is a dramatic looking shot and I''m sure it will do decently.</td>', 'This is obviously from someone who has never gotten one of my infamous JPEG comments before. So, here you go... There are a ton of compression artifacts showing around the edges of the tower. A 39k file size confirms excessive compression is what is killing the detail and clarity in this shot. Compression kills detail. Always use the least amount of compression you can get away with and still come in under the challenge limit. Other than that it is a dramatic looking shot and I''m sure it will do decently.', '2010-01-18 22:11:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5817437, 846761, 30214, '<td valign="top">I am thinking, <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=69668" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">njsabs</a>... nice job Jennifer (assuming I am right), or whoever you are :)</td>', 'I am thinking,  njsabs... nice job Jennifer (assuming I am right), or whoever you are :)', '2010-01-18 22:11:57.000000', NULL, 1),
