(5819742, 846600, 103142, '<td valign="top">It was the man on the right that did it for me. They were so wonderfully clear and he was just a passing shadow. I wasn''t sure if you were panning, or if he was just moving faster, or if it was the depth of field -- I had no idea!<br/> <br/>I actually wondered about this one being yours, but it wasn''t black and white! Anyway, enough rambling! This was definitely one of my favs of the challenge, and it desperately needs a bluebird!<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=811107" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/103142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_811107.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/103142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_811107.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/103142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_811107.jpg"/></a> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=935058&amp;page=1#5819711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">link to the posthumous thread</a></td>', 'It was the man on the right that did it for me. They were so wonderfully clear and he was just a passing shadow. I wasn''t sure if you were panning, or if he was just moving faster, or if it was the depth of field -- I had no idea! I actually wondered about this one being yours, but it wasn''t black and white! Anyway, enough rambling! This was definitely one of my favs of the challenge, and it desperately needs a bluebird!  link to the posthumous thread', '2010-01-20 13:35:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5819786, 845105, 100831, '<td valign="top">Your 5 ones were at least balanced by five tens!<br/>I agree that the best way to improve is to study your own work but also to study others.<br/>Take a concentrated look at photos that really appeal to you - things like exposure, color, composition, and then try and think what you could do to make your own shots better. (I also find commenting helps me because I''m forced to think).<br/>Even the photographers who get the high scoring shots keep looking for ways to improve.<br/>The other thing to keep in mind is that score isn''t everything. People like different things and people vote in different manners. Concentrate on making what you do the best you can make it first.</td>', 'Your 5 ones were at least balanced by five tens!I agree that the best way to improve is to study your own work but also to study others.Take a concentrated look at photos that really appeal to you - things like exposure, color, composition, and then try and think what you could do to make your own shots better. (I also find commenting helps me because I''m forced to think).Even the photographers who get the high scoring shots keep looking for ways to improve.The other thing to keep in mind is that score isn''t everything. People like different things and people vote in different manners. Concentrate on making what you do the best you can make it first.', '2010-01-20 14:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5819801, 845105, 112136, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>.......Take a concentrated look at photos that really appeal to you - things like exposure, color, composition, and then try and think what you could do to make your own shots better. (I also find commenting helps me because I''m forced to think).<br/>Even the photographers who get the high scoring shots keep looking for ways to improve.<br/>.....Concentrate on making what you do the best you can make it first. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agreed..<br/>Thanks penny :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyStreet: .......Take a concentrated look at photos that really appeal to you - things like exposure, color, composition, and then try and think what you could do to make your own shots better. (I also find commenting helps me because I''m forced to think).Even the photographers who get the high scoring shots keep looking for ways to improve......Concentrate on making what you do the best you can make it first.   Agreed..Thanks penny :-)', '2010-01-20 14:17:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5819805, 845105, 112136, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> Saw you thread.  ''1''s happen all the time, and you need to understand that many different people from very different backgrounds vote on challenges here.   <br/> <br/>Your photo appears to be a bit overexposed, its not completely sharp in focus on the face, and the blade of grass across the front is a bit distracting.  Close up insect shots are very common on DPC these days and those entered need to have WOW to score well.<br/> <br/>While I would not vote this a 1, I don''t think it is one of the better images in the challenge and would likely have voted it a 3 or 4 for the reasons stated above. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The grass-blade, and overexposure was intentional.<br/>but lack of focus is a flaw really. <br/>Thanks</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone: Saw you thread.  ''1''s happen all the time, and you need to understand that many different people from very different backgrounds vote on challenges here.    Your photo appears to be a bit overexposed, its not completely sharp in focus on the face, and the blade of grass across the front is a bit distracting.  Close up insect shots are very common on DPC these days and those entered need to have WOW to score well. While I would not vote this a 1, I don''t think it is one of the better images in the challenge and would likely have voted it a 3 or 4 for the reasons stated above.   The grass-blade, and overexposure was intentional.but lack of focus is a flaw really. Thanks', '2010-01-20 14:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
