(5826274, 846552, 90495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cboydrun:</b></div><hr/><i> the border takes away from the photo... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I beg to differ. <br/> <br/>Nice shot, not a typical action shot though since there''s not much action going on. I like the colours and his pose and smile tells me he''s having fun. Technically, I have nothing to say about it, all well done.</td>', 'Originally posted by Cboydrun: the border takes away from the photo...   I beg to differ.  Nice shot, not a typical action shot though since there''s not much action going on. I like the colours and his pose and smile tells me he''s having fun. Technically, I have nothing to say about it, all well done.', '2010-01-23 09:24:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5826305, 846245, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB</b> <br/>There are times when <b>I</b> don''t know why the voters elect to give middling scores to a good image.  This is one of them.<br/> <br/>I think your processing is fine, delicate and carefully done.  Fabulous sunrise, captured and processed well, with nice tones in the buildings and street lights complementing that early light.  It is perhaps more illustration-like than ''realistic'' photography, but that suits the image.  <br/> <br/>Maybe a sleepy kid in a red coat with a sled dragging behind would have added punch - (I''m really fantasizing here) but in any event I think you did a good job and can only say:  "Keep up the good work!"<br/> <br/>PS  I gave you a ''7'' in competition for this Xmas Card type image.<br/> <br/></td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB There are times when I don''t know why the voters elect to give middling scores to a good image.  This is one of them. I think your processing is fine, delicate and carefully done.  Fabulous sunrise, captured and processed well, with nice tones in the buildings and street lights complementing that early light.  It is perhaps more illustration-like than ''realistic'' photography, but that suits the image.   Maybe a sleepy kid in a red coat with a sled dragging behind would have added punch - (I''m really fantasizing here) but in any event I think you did a good job and can only say:  "Keep up the good work!" PS  I gave you a ''7'' in competition for this Xmas Card type image. ', '2010-01-23 09:32:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5826337, 846714, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB</b> <br/> <br/>What a good looking model you have selected for this image.  She has poise and flair and it comes across well here.<br/> <br/>Obviously you are going for the Candid style and have succeeded.  <br/> <br/>In the ''critique'' area, (which is why I''m here) the image looks a bit unbalanced with the crop just below the knees. I would also suggest that even with candids, too much background clutter can take away from the main subject.  The background chairs, the nearly hidden figure directly behind your subject - just a little change in your position might have made a difference in the overall image.  <br/> <br/>Nevertheless, you caught a special moment and a priceless expression on the young model''s face.  And that makes this image special.</td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB  What a good looking model you have selected for this image.  She has poise and flair and it comes across well here. Obviously you are going for the Candid style and have succeeded.   In the ''critique'' area, (which is why I''m here) the image looks a bit unbalanced with the crop just below the knees. I would also suggest that even with candids, too much background clutter can take away from the main subject.  The background chairs, the nearly hidden figure directly behind your subject - just a little change in your position might have made a difference in the overall image.   Nevertheless, you caught a special moment and a priceless expression on the young model''s face.  And that makes this image special.', '2010-01-23 09:46:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5826419, 846552, 42256, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jac:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cboydrun:</b></div><hr/><i> the border takes away from the photo... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I beg to differ. <br/> <br/>Nice shot, not a typical action shot though since there''s not much action going on. I like the colours and his pose and smile tells me he''s having fun. Technically, I have nothing to say about it, all well done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Look at the last comments by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=80878" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Cboydrun</a>.. looks like he is obsessed with borders! <br/> <br/>As for this picture, I like the composition, shallow dof and the nice stop action.  What I don''t like is the lack of sharpness. Background is a little distracting, and looking at the color of ice, it seems underexposed a tad bit.</td>', 'Originally posted by Jac: Originally posted by Cboydrun: the border takes away from the photo...   I beg to differ.  Nice shot, not a typical action shot though since there''s not much action going on. I like the colours and his pose and smile tells me he''s having fun. Technically, I have nothing to say about it, all well done.   Look at the last comments by  Cboydrun.. looks like he is obsessed with borders!  As for this picture, I like the composition, shallow dof and the nice stop action.  What I don''t like is the lack of sharpness. Background is a little distracting, and looking at the color of ice, it seems underexposed a tad bit.', '2010-01-23 10:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5826706, 846552, 67697, '<td valign="top">I thought this might have been yours lol.  I should have said so - oh well.  I thought the Topaz was done well.  I could tell it was there but that''s only because I use it so much.  I like how you used the software to make his details stand out some more.  <br/> <br/>I did give it a 6 because after admiring the topaz work (lol) I didn''t see more of a story to pull me in.  I guess I''ve become DPC-ified and I was looking for drama :D<br/> <br/>Oh and the reason why I thought it might have been yours (beyond the Topaz) was because your people portraits either have a sense of irony or there''s a subtle quirkiness about it (and that is what this photo has).</td>', 'I thought this might have been yours lol.  I should have said so - oh well.  I thought the Topaz was done well.  I could tell it was there but that''s only because I use it so much.  I like how you used the software to make his details stand out some more.   I did give it a 6 because after admiring the topaz work (lol) I didn''t see more of a story to pull me in.  I guess I''ve become DPC-ified and I was looking for drama :D Oh and the reason why I thought it might have been yours (beyond the Topaz) was because your people portraits either have a sense of irony or there''s a subtle quirkiness about it (and that is what this photo has).', '2010-01-23 11:31:52.000000', NULL, 0),
